From ec61ac6d55675a89bb3fdb619b6b076abfe44f3c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ritvik <ritvik2014@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 18:36:38 +0400
Subject: [PATCH 36/38] auto-fit: columns size themselves as windows come and
 go

layout { auto-fit-columns true; } (off by default, so upstream behaviour and
tests are unchanged): alone a column fills the screen; beside others a
window keeps its rule width (Zen 2/3 + terminal 1/3) when those fit
together, else they share evenly; full-width rules stay full; a column you
size by hand (set-column-width, presets, mouse resize, expand) is left
alone until the new auto-fit-columns action hands it back. Maximize and
fullscreen don't pin.

Smooth by construction: a new window's first configure already carries its
fitted width, its neighbours are resized in the same step, and the view
target is computed from the widths columns are heading to, so a new window
never opens wide, scrolls, then corrects. Runs only when columns come and
go: one allocation-free pass over the workspace's columns.
